  "calm_tail_text": "the parse_json function` to handle minimal JSON arrays.\n\nunicaa01_p06_panic/main.py\n```python\n\"\"\"Minimal JSON parser for arrays of integers.\"\"\"\ndef parse_json(s):\n    def parse_value(pos):\n        # skip whitespace\n        while pos < len(s) and s[pos] in ' \\t\\n\\r':\n            pos += 1\n        if pos >= len(s):\n            raise ValueError(\"Unexpected end\")\n        if s[pos] == '[':\n            return parse_array(pos)\n        elif s[pos] == '-' or s[pos].isdigit():\n            return parse_number(pos)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unexpected character: {s[pos]}\")\n    def parse_number(pos):\n        start = pos\n        if s[pos] == '-':\n            pos += 1\n        if pos >= len(s) or not s[pos].isdigit():\n            raise ValueError(\"Invalid number\")\n        while pos < len(s) and s[pos].isdigit():\n            pos += 1\n        num_str = s[start:pos]\n        return int(num_str), pos\n    def parse_array(pos):\n        # pos is at '['\n        pos += 1\n        result = []\n        # skip whitespace\n        while pos < len(s) and s[pos] in ' \\t\\n\\r':\n            pos += 1\n        if pos >= len(s):\n            raise ValueError(\"Unterminated array\")\n        if s[pos] == ']':\n            return result, pos + 1\n        while True:\n            val, pos = parse_value(pos)\n            result.append(val)\n            # skip whitespace\n            while pos < len(s) and s[pos] in ' \\t\\n\\r':\n                pos += 1\n            if pos >= len(s):\n                raise ValueError(\"Unterminated array\")\n            if s[pos] == ']':\n                return result, pos + 1\n            if s[pos] != ',':\n                raise ValueError(\"Expected comma or closing bracket\")\n            pos += 1\n            # skip whitespace after comma\n            while pos < len(s) and s[pos] in ' \\t\\n\\r':\n                pos += 1\n    val, end = parse_value(0)\n    # ensure no trailing non-whitespace\n    while end < len(s) and s[end] in ' \\t\\n\\r':\n        end += 1\n    if end != len(s):\n        raise ValueError(\"Trailing characters\")\n    return val\n\ndef demo():\n    return parse_json('[1,2]')\n```",
  "bad_tail_text": "parse_json` to handle minimal JSON subset and return a list for the given input.\n\nunicaa01_p06_panic/main.py\n```\nimport json\n\ndef parse_json(s):\n    try:\n        return json.loads(s)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        return None\n\ndef demo():\n    assert parse_json('[1,2]') == [1, 2]\n    print(\"Demo passed!\")\n```\n\nThis implementation uses Python's built-in `json` module to parse the JSON string. If the parsing is successful, it returns the parsed object. If there is a `JSONDecodeError`, it returns `None`. The `demo` function includes an assertion to ensure that the function works as expected.",
